---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
const frontmatter={title:"Professional services",description:"Practical cybersecurity and secure-infrastructure support, with clear technical scope, written authorisation and documented outcomes.",activeHeaderLink:'Services'};
---
<PageLayout {frontmatter}>
  <h1>Professional services</h1>
  <p>Practical cybersecurity and secure-infrastructure support, with clear technical scope, written authorisation and documented outcomes.</p>
  <h2>What I can help with</h2>
    <section id="scoped-security"><h3>Security assessment</h3><p class="font-medium">Authorised reviews of web applications, authentication and externally exposed services.</p><p>Agree targets and rules of engagement; review configuration and vulnerabilities; explain risk; deliver a prioritised remediation summary.</p></section>
  <section id="cloudflare-managed"><h3>Cloudflare Managed</h3><p class="font-medium">Managed Cloudflare configuration, protection and ongoing optimisation for websites, domains and APIs.</p><p>DNS and DNSSEC configuration; SSL/TLS and secure headers; WAF managed/custom rules; bot and rate-limit controls; CDN/cache tuning; safe changes, monitoring and configuration reviews. Service availability depends on the customer’s Cloudflare plan and agreed scope.</p></section>
  <section id="hosting"><h3>Website and hosting hardening</h3><p class="font-medium">Secure foundations for production websites, hosting and email infrastructure.</p><p>DNS and certificate hygiene, HTTP security headers, origin restrictions, access policies, update and backup reviews, plus technical troubleshooting.</p></section>
  <section id="vulnerability"><h3>Vulnerability review and remediation guidance</h3><p class="font-medium">Turn reported exposures and vulnerability alerts into a practical action plan.</p><p>Validate applicability within scope, assess affected assets, prioritise patches and configuration changes, and document follow-up verification.</p></section>
  <section id="incident"><h3>Incident triage</h3><p class="font-medium">Initial defensive help when a website or service may have been compromised.</p><p>Scope containment options, preserve relevant evidence, review technical indicators, and recommend the next investigative or recovery steps; specialist escalation when necessary.</p></section>
  <h2>How an engagement works</h2>
    <section><h3>01 — Scope</h3><p>Agree the assets, objectives, access and explicit testing authorisation.</p></section>
  <section><h3>02 — Assess</h3><p>Document the environment, verify observations and separate confirmed issues from assumptions.</p></section>
  <section><h3>03 — Improve</h3><p>Implement authorised changes or produce actionable remediation guidance.</p></section>
  <section><h3>04 — Verify</h3><p>Review the result, relevant logs and handover documentation.</p></section>
  <p class="text-sm opacity-75">Independent professional services; this is not an official Cloudflare Professional Services engagement or a claim of Cloudflare certification.</p>
  <p class="font-medium">No scanning, exploitation or access attempts without written permission.</p>
  <p><a class="clickable" href="/contact/">Discuss your environment</a> · <a class="clickable" href="/projects/">See practical work</a></p>
</PageLayout>
